ings\""}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0377-514ab27efa21:d04", "start": 0, "end": 614, "text": "Toggle the table of contents Revisited (Frank Sinatra album) Add languages Add links Article Talk English Read Edit View history Tools Tools move to sidebar hide Actions Read Edit View history General What links here Related changes Upload file Permanent link Page information Cite this page Get shortened URL Download QR code Print/export Download as PDF Printable version In other projects Wikidata item Appearance move to sidebar hide From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia 1960 studio album by Frank Sinatra Revisited Studio album by Frank Sinatra Released 1960 Recorded March and April 1960 at the Fine Studio,"}, "D6S1": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0377-514ab27efa21:d05", "start": 0, "end": 151, "text": "Revisited (Tom Lehrer album) Revisited is a 1960 album by Tom Lehrer, consisting of live recordings of all the songs from 1953's \"Songs by Tom Lehrer\"."}, "D6S2": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0377-514ab27efa21:d05", "start": 152, "end": 337, "text": "The CD reissue of the album contains two additional tracks that Lehrer wrote and performed for the PBS television show \"The Electric Company\" (and produced and conducted by Joe Raposo)."}, "D6S3": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0377-514ab27efa21:d05", "start": 338, "end": 590, "text": "On the original Lehrer Records release of \"Revisited\", tracks 1–6 (side 1) were recorded live on November 23 & 24, 1959, in Kresge Auditorium at MIT in Cambridge, MA, while tracks 7–13 (side 2) were recorded live at two concerts during Lehrer's tour of"}, "D7S1": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0377-514ab27efa21:d06", "start": 0, "end": 448, "text": "Lockie, who by 1981 joined Public Image Ltd.; Keith Levene, also of Public Image; Jimmy Hughes, ex-The Banned, and later in Department S; Terry Chimes, ex-The Clash and later with Generation X, Hanoi Rocks and Black Sabbath; Pa